# Art Asset Discovery

In the **Cursor IDE**, file-search has failed to surface binary files: a `**/*.png`
glob once returned 0 results even though 161 PNGs exist. The cause is Cursor not
indexing gitignored paths (the `import_tiles*/` pools and other assets), not the
files being absent. In Cursor, do NOT conclude an asset is missing from a 0-result
glob — fall back to the manifest below. (Other tools, e.g. Claude Code, glob these
files fine; this caveat is Cursor-specific.)

## Rules

1. To find art reliably across tools, consult [art-manifest.md](mdc:art-manifest.md) —
   the authoritative directory of every art/metadata file in the project (and the
   only dependable index inside Cursor).
2. Every asset is a pair: `Name.png` (Aseprite-exported image) + `Name.json`
   (frame/animation metadata). Treat them as a unit - move/copy both together.
3. If a file listed in the manifest seems missing, verify with the Read tool on the
   exact path (Read handles images) before claiming it doesn't exist.
4. After adding, removing, or moving any assets, regenerate the manifest:
   `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools/generate-art-manifest.ps1`
   (run with full permissions - the sandboxed shell silently no-ops on this machine).

## Folder policy

- `import_tiles/`, `import_tiles_enemy/`, `import_tiles_tools/` are a quarantined
  review pool from a previous game. They are gitignored (local-only, never pushed).
  Do NOT use them in the game directly and do NOT modify them.
- Art may only be used after the user reviews and approves it; approved pairs get
  copied into `assets/art/`, which is the only art folder the game loads from.
